## Context

Reuse the Vietnam pilot interfaces for the South African official register/report inventories; register categories and start dates are not automatically transactions.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

A register start date and allocation share a project with a separately documented payment. Migration must retain reported positions and establish only the evidenced payment event, with no duplicate amount.

## Actions

Pin the selected official report/register editions, enumerate their inventories and reconcile all ZAF legacy rows. Preserve programme/components, agreement references and uncertain dates. Record source-regime mapping decisions and unresolved finance. Provide candidate semantic/payload-size report with the old public contract.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Official and legacy rows have complete disposition reports
- [ ] Register dates and financial categories retain source meaning
- [ ] IDs/routes/relationships survive without programme-component double counting
- [ ] Candidate payload respects file limit or waits for compatible chunking before publication

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

